WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.520
An electrode contacts the body; a lead is the electrical view calculated from electrode signals. A standard twelve-lead ECG uses ten electrodes to create twelve views. Limb leads are not excluded from the diagnostic ECG merely because lead two is also commonly used for rhythm monitoring.
电极接触身体，导联则是从电极信号计算出的电观察方向。标准十二导联用10个电极形成12个视角。II 导联常用于节律监护，并不意味着肢体导联不属于诊断性心电图。

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:39.048
Bipolar limb leads compare two poles. Augmented limb and precordial leads use a positive exploring electrode and a calculated reference. The same activation sequence can therefore appear upright in one lead and negative in another without representing two different heartbeats.
双极肢体导联比较两极；加压肢体导联和胸前导联则使用正向探查电极与计算参考。因此，同一次激动在一个导联向上、另一个向下，并不代表两个不同的心搏。

00:00:39.048 --> 00:01:01.584
Continuous monitoring tracks rate and rhythm over time, commonly displaying lead two or a modified chest lead. Diagnostic twelve-lead acquisition records multiple anatomical views with suitable quality and filter settings. The difference is purpose and acquisition configuration, not a rule that certain standard leads are monitoring-only.
连续监护追踪心率、节律，常显示 II 导联或改良胸导联；诊断性十二导联则用适当质量与滤波设置记录多个解剖视角。区别在用途和采集配置，不是某些标准导联只能用于监护。

00:01:01.584 --> 00:01:23.760
MCL1 is near a V1 monitoring viewpoint and MCL6 near V6, but their configuration and reference differ from a standard diagnostic recording. Follow the device instructions and local protocol. Never relabel a modified monitoring view as a correctly acquired standard twelve-lead ECG.
MCL1 接近 V1 监护视角，MCL6 接近 V6，但其配置与参考方式不同于标准诊断记录。应按设备说明及本地流程使用，不能把改良监护视图重新命名为技术正确的标准十二导联。

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:43.128
Explain the procedure and seek cooperation before exposing the chest. Maintain draping and reveal only the area needed. For a patient with breasts, use the correct chest-wall landmarks rather than placing electrodes on breast tissue when feasible, while preserving dignity and consent.
暴露胸部前解释操作并征求配合，保持遮盖，只暴露所需部位。对有乳房的患者，应在可行时依据正确胸壁标志放置，而不是贴在乳房组织上，同时维护尊严与同意。

00:01:43.128 --> 00:02:03.240
A history of trauma, cultural concerns, pain or patient preference may affect placement. Discuss a workable approach without coercion. Document any declined or modified placement and its interpretive limitation, rather than quietly treating a nonstandard recording as standard.
创伤经历、文化顾虑、疼痛或患者意愿可能影响放置。应讨论可行方案，不能强迫。对拒绝或修改的位置及其判读局限要记录，不能悄悄把非标准记录当标准记录。

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:23.160
Place limb electrodes on appropriate clean, flat limb areas, avoiding poor contact over bone or joints. The school uses the AHA colour convention: right arm white, left arm black, right leg green and left leg red. Read the cable labels because other colour systems exist.
肢体电极放在适当、清洁平坦的肢体部位，避免骨突或关节处接触不良。学校使用 AHA 配色：右臂白、左臂黑、右腿绿、左腿红；其他配色系统也存在，因此应读取线缆标签。

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:44.136
Limb reversal or unrecorded relocation can change axis and waveform appearance. If a tracing differs unexpectedly, recheck connections and anatomy before assuming a new disease. A genuine negative QRS may still be physiological or pathological after placement has been verified.
肢体接反或未记录的位置改变会影响电轴和波形。若记录意外变化，应先复核连接和解剖位置，不能立即假定新疾病；但位置确认后，负向 QRS 仍可能是真实生理或病理表现。

00:02:44.136 --> 00:03:04.968
Identify ribs from anatomical landmarks rather than estimating by eye. Place V1 at the fourth intercostal space on the right sternal border and V2 at the fourth space on the left. Locate V4 at the fifth intercostal space on the midclavicular line before positioning V3 between V2 and V4.
应利用解剖标志辨认肋骨，而不是目测。V1 位于右胸骨缘第4肋间，V2 位于左胸骨缘第4肋间；先找到锁骨中线第5肋间的 V4，再把 V3 放在 V2、V4 中点。

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:23.712
V5 lies on the anterior axillary line and V6 on the midaxillary line, both horizontally level with V4. Do not follow the rib space downward around the chest. Check all six positions before acquiring, and document unavoidable departures from standard placement.
V5 位于腋前线，V6 位于腋中线，二者都与 V4 保持同一水平。不要沿肋间向胸侧下斜排列。采集前核对六个位置，并记录无法避免的非标准放置。

00:03:23.712 --> 00:03:43.608
When the net depolarization vector moves toward a lead’s positive viewpoint, it tends to produce an upward deflection; movement away tends downward. Lead two commonly aligns with normal ventricular activation, which explains its usefulness, but it is not guaranteed to be the largest or always upright.
净去极化向量朝某导联正向视角运动时，通常产生向上偏转；背离时通常向下。II 导联常与正常心室激动方向较一致，因此很实用，但不保证其振幅最大，也不保证永远向上。

00:03:43.608 --> 00:04:01.632
Unexpected polarity is a reason to inspect placement and connections, not a command to rearrange electrodes until the tracing looks normal. Once technical errors are corrected, preserve the real finding, obtain appropriate additional views and integrate the patient’s condition.
意外极性变化意味着应检查位置和连接，不是要求不断移动电极直到波形“正常”。纠正技术错误后，应保留真实发现，取得适当补充视角，并结合患者状况解释。
